there's this car that's
typically parked there

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.540
that has a vanity license plate.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.200
You know me and my Bumper Stumpers,

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.078
I always notice the vanity license plates

00:11:25.078 --> 00:11:28.290
and there's a license
plate that said Mr. Noodle.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.193
- Oh.
- Which,

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:33.427
for those of you who don't know,
Mr. Noodle is a live action

00:11:33.427 --> 00:11:38.427
mime character in Elmo's World,
the Sesame Street series,

00:11:38.763 --> 00:11:41.330
and he was kinda like
a clown without makeup.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.850
He would do clownish things

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:47.510
and then Mr. Noodle had
a brother Mr. Noodle

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.490
and Elmo would voiceover this whole,

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.560
you know Mr. Noodle, right?

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.880
- Never watched it.
- Lily was really into Elmo,

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.770
I think Lincoln was too.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.350
- I saw the controversy
come and never let my kids,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.570
I just sensed it, never let 'em watch it.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.403
- Oh.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.513
I separate the man from the puppet.

00:12:04.513 --> 00:12:07.180
- That's a difficult thing to
do when his hand is in there.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:09.335
(Link chuckles)

00:12:09.335 --> 00:12:11.660
(both chuckling)

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.170
Pretty much becomes a dead Elmo

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.519
when you take him out of the--

00:12:14.519 --> 00:12:17.269
(Link chuckling)

00:12:18.515 --> 00:12:20.791
- Okay good point, I
have no response to that.

00:12:20.791 --> 00:12:22.913
I'm not even gonna tell my story now.

00:12:26.765 --> 00:12:31.350
So I will clarify that
there are no controversies

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.030
that I know of associated with Mr. Noodle

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.090
or his brother Mr. Noodle.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.129
- Even though with that name
you would think there would be.

00:12:36.129 --> 00:12:37.903
- Right.
(both laughing)

00:12:37.903 --> 00:12:40.750
- If anybody's problematic,
it's probably Mr. Noodle.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:41.583
- Right.

00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:44.907
Mr. Noodle's brother
Mr. Noodle was played by

00:12:44.907 --> 00:12:48.220
the guy from Evening Shade who--

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:49.790
- Oh I loved that.
- Who was also in

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.543
The Green Mile but I
can't be more specific

00:12:51.543 --> 00:12:53.430
about what his name is but anyway--

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:54.880
- Mustache.
- So this license plate

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.330
Mr. Noodle and then sometimes
but on a rare occasion,

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:01.660
I'll see another car and it says,

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.020
the license plate said Dr. Noodle.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.690
I'm like oh there's a family of Noodles

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:07.100
that live around here.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:10.480
- What?
- And so for like two years,

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:13.630
I've seen these vanity license plates,

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.082
and so it's just a part of my life.

00:13:15.082 --> 00:13:17.880
And sometimes we'll point it out,

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.003
there's Mr. Noodle's parked there again.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:24.710
That's just a little background.

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.590
So we're walking and now
I've got this poop bag

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.740
in my hand and Lily and I are walking.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.810
I'm catching her up on the
situation at the hospital

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:32.780
and everything, we're
having a great conversation,

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:35.799
but I'm bothered by the fact
that I haven't even completed

00:13:35.799 --> 00:13:40.799
30% of this dog walk and I'm
already holding poop in a bag.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:44.010
I do not like being that guy.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:47.570
I judge heavily the people
I see walking their dog

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:50.420
with a big sack of poop in their hand.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.150
- Right, you gotta offload that.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:55.000
- What a loser, but I also,

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.363
I hate seeing poop bags
just laying around.

00:13:58.304 --> 00:14:00.890
We are humans, you know.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.760
We're at a point on the
food chain where we need

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.300
to love our earth to
the point where we can't

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:10.250
just throw plastic poop bags
down just because of pride.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.940
- You see people throw
plastic poop bags down?

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:15.090
- I see them laying down, I see evidence

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.670
that they've been left places.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.550
Like when you go on hikes around LA,

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.850
there's people who will
drop their poop bag,

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.030
and you know what they're thinking?

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:24.250
They're thinking, I hate
walking around with a poop bag.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.290
When I come back down the
trail, I'll pick it up

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.510
and throw it away.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.699
No, you don't.
- And then when they see it,

00:14:29.699 --> 00:14:31.327
they're like, well, that
could be anybody's poop bag.

00:14:31.327 --> 00:14:32.160
- It's not mine.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.390
Oh yeah you conveniently forget about it.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.760
I don't wanna be that guy so
I'm in a catch 22 situation,

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:38.193
so I tell Lily, I'm like, Lily.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.860
When I spot a trash can,

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.840
you're gonna get rid of this thing.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.619
Now the trash had come
recently so it wasn't like

00:14:46.619 --> 00:14:48.720
everyone's trash cans were out.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.290
- But there are the stragglers.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.690
- There's some stragglers
and you're looking for that.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:52.530
- One out of 10.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.140
- So I'm like we're
looking for stragglers.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.000
We round this corner and go
down this other dead end street.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.210
I'm talking to her like
this and she's looking at me

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.287
like, you okay?

00:15:00.287 --> 00:15:03.616
- And let me say before you proceed,

00:15:03.616 --> 00:15:05.530
I believe in this.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.650
I'll just say that.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.530
I believe in what you're about to do.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.790
- Here's what I believe in.
- Okay.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.180
Because we're all humans.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.960
It's a public service.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.450
Yes it's your trash can but
I'm not changing the dynamics

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:23.556
of your trash, you know I'm
not throwing a chair in there.

00:15:23.556 --> 00:15:25.890
You know what I'm sayin'?
- Or a dead body.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:29.120
- It's a bag of poop, it
doesn't change anything.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.530
You should be okay with it.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.140
When you're--
- Subject, okay,

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:36.380
I'm glad you're backing me up but subject

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:39.047
to some specific key points that I believe

00:15:39.047 --> 00:15:41.660
and that I wanted to relay to Lily

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:42.943
'cause I needed her help.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.240
I think the first thing is,

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.980
you gotta pick the right trash can.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.910
There's a green one for--

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.210
- Oh of course.
- There's a blue one

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.780
for recycling, there's a black one.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.530
And I'm like Lily, look up there.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:55.990
I see some stragglers.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:57.240
There's three trash cans.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:00.010
What I want you to do and
this is my second point is--

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.430
- You're making your daughter do it?

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.471
- We gotta, the second point
is we gotta be clandestine.

00:16:04.471 --> 00:16:06.110
You gotta be secret.
- You gotta be sneaky.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.620
Even though I completely believe in it,

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:09.360
you still gotta be sneaky.
- 'Cause you never know

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.810
how a person's gonna feel
looking out their window

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:13.610
and seeing somebody open their trash can

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.990
and make a little deposit.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.610
You don't know if they're gonna run out

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:20.435
with some sort of a firearm or at least--

00:16:20.435 --> 00:16:21.268
- I doubt that would happen.

00:16:21.268 --> 00:16:23.740
- Armed to the gills with insults.

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.930
- That could happen.
- In front of my daughter

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:29.050
and my beloved beast, Jade.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.690
- 'Cause I will say that
if I saw it happen--

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.640
- You'd be mad.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.270
You would feel anger instinctively.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:35.560
- But I wouldn't say
anything 'cause I'd be like,

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.920
you know what, for all
the reasons I just said.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:38.753
But I understand--

00:16:38.753 --> 00:16:39.660
- But your heart rate would go up

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.230
and you'd have to do some breathing.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.523
- The tendency to be protective
of your trash, I get it.

00:16:43.523 --> 00:16:45.260
- It's your domain.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.960
- It's not logical but I get it.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:51.889
- So I'm like Lily,
we're gonna subtly scoot

00:16:51.889 --> 00:16:54.050
over to the left side of the road.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.670
As we're walking, we're
not gonna stop walking.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.040
I want you to go up to the trash can,

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.140
I want you to gently lift
the lid like three inches.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.860
All right, you don't have
to open it all the way.

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.050
I'm talking to her this way.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.660
- This may be over instruction but okay.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.320
- I'm like I just want you to just give me

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:10.880
a little poop bag gap and
then I'm gonna come in,

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.450
I'm gonna swoop in and I'm just gonna,

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:13.715
I'm gonna throw it in there--
- Hold on.

00:17:13.715 --> 00:17:14.548
- And then you just gently let go.

00:17:14.548 --> 00:17:16.270
- You made this a two person job?

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:17.538
- It has to be a two person job.

00:17:17.538 --> 00:17:19.508
- If I was there I would have
been like this is a bad idea.

00:17:19.508 --> 00:17:21.815
- Listen, you short-sighted amateur.

00:17:21.815 --> 00:17:23.570
(Rhett chuckles)

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:25.740
I'm walking a dog with
a leash in one hand,

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.640
I got poop in a bag in the other hand

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:29.570
and I got a daughter with two free hands.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:31.780
I gotta teach her the ways, man.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.290
This is a teachable moment.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:34.760
This is less about what I need

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:35.960
and more about what she needs.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:38.030
- I would give her the poop

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.800
and let her do the whole shebang.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.030
That's just what I would have done.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.380
- Well that's because--
- Two hands.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:43.860
- You're a cruel, unfeeling father.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.830
- Lift with one, deposit with the other,

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.360
and she's also a young woman--

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:49.370
- I lead by example.
- Which I think gives her,

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.640
she's gonna get a little more leeway,

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:52.320
they're gonna be a little bit less likely

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:55.340
to come out cussing or with a firearm.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.410
- Little less likely so
there's still a likelihood

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:02.090
that your daughter could be
blasted with poop bag insults.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.820
And hey, if you're fine with that,

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.170
your daughter can be thrown to the wolves.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.240
- Then she could be taught a lesson

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.490
and that would be the lesson.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:09.620
How do you deal with that?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:12.940
- So I'm like, I just need three inches.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:16.270
And three seconds and I'll
take care of the rest.

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:18.710
And she's like, Dad, this isn't a heist.

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:19.543
- Yeah.

00:18:19.543 --> 00:18:20.610
(Link chuckles)

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:21.810
I'm with her.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.130
- I'm like sh, we're almost there.

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.685
Just don't, just do the plan.

00:18:26.685 --> 00:18:27.600
(soft bass music)

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.120
And I'm talkin' like this now.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:30.953
And--

00:18:30.953 --> 00:18:32.190
- You probably look
suspicious, by the way.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.834
- And then she grabs the green.

00:18:34.834 --> 00:18:36.400
- The wrong one.
- No don't don't don't,

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.840
you gotta go with the black one.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.538
You gotta go to the black,
and then she gives me

00:18:40.538 --> 00:18:43.653
three inches on the black one
and I just make the deposit.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.720
And then phew, we
immediately swing back over

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.690
to the other side of the
road and I'm like yes.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.150
I think I literally out loud said yes.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:53.983
- Yeah.

00:18:53.983 --> 00:18:58.190
- And at that moment, I
looked up and I saw a car

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.880
with a person inside of
it and the door was open.

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.930
And I was like oh crap,
there's somebody there,

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.330
I think they saw us and I'm
like oh, nope, he didn't see us.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:10.920
He was in his car detailing his dash.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.320
- But he was the owner of the trash can.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:15.640
- He was on the same
side of the trash can.

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:19.820
I would say most likely the man
in the car cleaning the dash

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.730
was the owner of the
three trash cans, yes.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:23.563
- [Rhett] Mm-hmm.

00:19:23.563 --> 00:19:24.810
- I panic for a moment.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:26.962
- But as I stated before,
not really the owner.

00:19:26.962 --> 00:19:29.980
They're on loan from the city.
- He's renting it.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:31.880
- Yeah so we're all paying for it.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.560
- Put yourself in his shoes, Rhett.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.337
I was a bit afraid until I
realized and I told Lily,

00:19:36.337 --> 00:19:37.617
"He didn't see it.

00:19:37.617 --> 00:19:40.767
"He didn't see anything,
we have succeeded.

00:19:40.767 --> 00:19:42.517
"We are amazing.

00:19:42.517 --> 00:19:44.517
"You know what, I hope Jade craps again.

00:19:45.627 --> 00:19:47.360
"Right now so we can just do it again."

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.683
It was exhilarating.

00:19:49.657 --> 00:19:51.330
I was like on the edge.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.910
The dude was like rubbin' his dash down

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.330
with some Armor All situation.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:20:00.270
He was like me when I first
got my 1987 Nissan pickup

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:01.907
and I thought that I was gonna wax it

00:20:01.907 --> 00:20:04.920
and it was already so
old that when I waxed it,

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:06.467
it basically just took
the paint off of it.

00:20:06.467 --> 00:20:08.828
- You saw chrome underneath.
- Yeah.

00:20:08.828 --> 00:20:10.830
It was like sheer metal.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.040
The dude was going at
it, he never looked up.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:15.203
I was like, oh, that's your fault, man.

00:20:16.959 --> 00:20:20.525
You're too into your dash to
see who's making the stash

00:20:20.525 --> 00:20:23.000
in your can.
- Okay, what happened though?

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.900
- Okay yeah I should
get on with this story.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.140
So I walk by and we go
all the way to the end

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.960
of the road and then
we have to turn around

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:31.040
and we're walking back and I'm like,

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.220
oh, the guy's still
there and then I noticed

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.820
from this new vantage point
I can see the license plate

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:40.280
on the car and it says Dr. Noodle.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:41.113
- Oh gosh.

00:20:41.113 --> 00:20:43.220
- So then without saying anything to Lily,

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:46.670
as we're walking by,
again his door's open,

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:50.130
one foot's out and he's
still on that dash,

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.124
just grinding it.

00:20:52.124 --> 00:20:53.462
He's just like--
- It's a dirty dash.

00:20:53.462 --> 00:20:56.363
- (chuckles) It was a
shiny dash by this point.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:01.880
We get up next to him
and I'm probably as far

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:04.020
from here to that wall
so like I don't know,

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:05.123
seven feet away.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:11.580
And at that point, without
really planning out

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.069
what I'm gonna do, I just
went with the feeling.

00:21:15.069 --> 00:21:15.902
- Surprise.

00:21:15.902 --> 00:21:18.830
- I was feeling on top of the
world after what had happened

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.923
and I point at him.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.947
And I say, "You must be Dr. Noodle."

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.443
And he looks up from his dash,

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:37.913
and the look on his
face went from surprise,

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:43.820
someone's speaking to me,
to jaw-dropping amazement

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:49.170
and he says, "You know me?"

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.753
(Rhett laughs)

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:58.660
And then, before I could
say anything in response,

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:02.771
he said, "I know you too."

00:22:02.771 --> 00:22:06.010
(Rhett laughs)

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.890
And I never stopped walking.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:08.723
- What?

00:22:08.723 --> 00:22:12.347
- I never stopped walking
and I said, "Cool, man.

00:22:12.347 --> 00:22:13.710
